# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# PRODUCTION ENVIRONMENT (Render.com deployment)
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# This file is used when building for production deployment
# Local API keys stay in .env.local (for testing)
# Render.com injects these from Dashboard (more secure)
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

# VA.gov OAuth - Production URLs
# IMPORTANT: This redirect URI must EXACTLY match what you registered
# on the VA sandbox access form at https://developer.va.gov/explore
VITE_VA_REDIRECT_URL=https://vet-rate.org/callback
VITE_VA_API_ENV=sandbox

# VA OAuth API Path — determines which VA API's OAuth server is used.
# Must match the API you registered for. Common paths:
#   veteran-verification/v1  (Service History & Eligibility, disability ratings)
#   claims/v1                (Benefits Claims)
#   clinical-health/v1       (Clinical Health / FHIR)
VITE_VA_OAUTH_API_PATH=veteran-verification/v1

# Note: Client ID and API keys are injected by Render from Dashboard
# Don't put sensitive values here if committing to git
